* Your TypeScript service passes manual testing but fails in production. How would you improve its automated test coverage?
* A unit test passes locally but fails in the CI/CD pipeline. How would you investigate the issue?
* Your test suite contains intermittent failures caused by asynchronous operations. How would you stabilize it?
* An API service depends on an external payment provider. How would you test its business logic without making real payments?
* Your application retries failed API requests several times. How would you verify retry counts, delays, and final error handling?
* A database repository is difficult to unit test because it creates its own database connection. How would you refactor it?
* Your service contains multiple dependencies, and mocking them makes the test difficult to maintain. How would you simplify the design?
* A developer changes a function signature, but the existing tests still pass despite incorrect behavior. How would you improve the tests?
* Your application has several conditional branches, but code coverage is low. How would you identify missing test cases?
* A function handles empty arrays, null values, and invalid input. How would you test all relevant edge cases?
* Your API response sometimes contains unexpected fields or missing properties. How would you test runtime validation?
* Your application processes messages from a queue. How would you test duplicate messages and message-processing failures?
* A background job must not process the same transaction twice. How would you test idempotency?
* Your service caches frequently requested data. How would you test cache hits, expiration, and invalidation?
* A scheduled task uses timers and runs at specific intervals. How would you test it without waiting for real time to pass?
* Your authentication service has different permissions for administrators and regular users. How would you test authorization rules?
* Your TypeScript application integrates with a third-party API that frequently changes. How would you detect contract changes early?
* A production bug was caused by an unhandled Promise rejection. How would you reproduce it and prevent recurrence?
* Your test suite takes 30 minutes to execute. How would you reduce its execution time without sacrificing important coverage?
* Multiple developers run tests in parallel, causing shared test data to conflict. How would you resolve the problem?
* Your tests depend on environment variables and behave differently across environments. How would you make them deterministic?
* A database integration test passes on one machine but fails on another. How would you investigate environmental dependencies?
* Your team wants to replace Jest with Vitest. What compatibility and migration issues would you evaluate?
* Your code coverage is 95%, but production defects remain frequent. How would you evaluate the quality of your tests?
* A service calls multiple downstream APIs, and one API failure should not break the entire workflow. How would you test partial failures?
* Your application must handle duplicate payment requests safely. How would you design unit and integration tests for idempotency?
* A TypeScript monorepo contains multiple packages with shared utilities. How would you test dependencies between packages?
* A bug appears only when two asynchronous operations finish in a particular order. How would you reproduce and test the race condition?
* Your application needs backward compatibility with older API clients. How would you create automated compatibility tests?
* How would you design a testing strategy for a high-volume enterprise TypeScript application before a major release?